From 88b8bae63d2949d9f2a90270880275bdab11c3a9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: atomozero <bernardi.andrea@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 22:00:28 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 07/42] gpio_leds, led_server: the Wi-Fi LED of the AC100 shows
 the link

gpio_leds is a driver for the LEDs a device tree describes as children of
a gpio-leds node: each one is published as /dev/misc/led/<label>, read
gives 0 or 1, writing 0 or 1 switches it off or on. It drives the pins
through the Tegra GPIO module and honours default-state.

led_server decides what the LEDs show: an LED named for Wi-Fi is on
while a wireless interface has a link, following the network
notifications. It quits at once on a machine without such LEDs, and is
started only where it is installed (ARM for now).

Signed-off-by: atomozero <bernardi.andrea@gmail.com>
